## FiveM Royale -- PUBLIC SERVER tunables
##
## This file deliberately sets nothing.
##
## Copy it onto the game box as  tunables.cfg  next to server.cfg. Every value
## then comes from br_lib/config/match.lua exactly as it is committed, which is
## what a public server should be running: the values that were reviewed, not
## the values somebody typed on a box once.
##
## It exists so that "make this the public server again" is one copy and a
## restart -- the same operation as "make this the dev server", in the other
## direction -- rather than a hunt through a file for lines to comment out.
##
## Not having a tunables.cfg on the box at all produces the same GAME. FXServer
## will complain once on start that it could not execute the file it was told
## to, and then carry on with every default in place. Shipping this file is how
## you get the silence as well.
##
## The dev settings, and what each one does, are documented in
## tunables.dev.cfg.example. If you want one of them on a public server, put it
## here on purpose -- and expect the boot banner to say so on every start.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# THE ONE THING THIS FILE DOES SET, and it sets it to the value a public server
# must have.
#
# Dev mode lowers the minimum players to start a match from 16 to 1 and unlocks
# the dev-only debug commands. It is not one of the tunables -- it is an older
# switch read by br_core/server/main.lua -- but it is the setting most likely to
# be left on by accident, and the whole point of this file is that copying it
# over tunables.cfg leaves you with a public server and nothing to remember.
#
# It is spelled out here rather than left absent BECAUSE ABSENT IS NOT ENOUGH:
# server.cfg.example ships with both of these set to true further down the
# file, and in a .cfg the last line wins. If your server.cfg still has them,
# delete those two lines -- otherwise they will quietly override these, and this
# file will have made a public server that starts matches with one player in it.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
set sv_devMode false
set br_devMode false

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# THE ADMIN CONSOLE is deliberately NOT set here, and this comment is the only
# thing about it in this file.
#
# br_adminConsoleUrl turns on the Admin tab in the pause menu (#23). It is off
# on a public server not because it would be unsafe -- the tab is shown only to
# licenses holding the console scope in DynamoDB, and the console runs its own
# live Discord role check before it will open a session -- but because a public
# box has no reason to carry the console's address at all.
#
# If you do want it on a public server, put it here on purpose, spelled the way
# tunables.dev.cfg.example documents, and expect the boot banner to say so on
# every start.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# OUR DISCORD is not set here either, and this one is worth a second look before
# you accept that.
#
# br_discordUrl is the address appended to the message a kicked or banned player
# sees ("Please join our Discord to discuss or appeal: ..."), and since
# 2026-08-30 it is also the Discord card in the pause menu -- a card every player
# can press to copy the invite, drawn only when this is set. Unlike everything
# else named in these two files it is NOT a dev-versus-public difference -- it
# is the same address on every box, and a public server is where the kicks
# actually happen and where the card is worth the most.
#
# It stays unset here because this file's whole promise is that copying it over
# tunables.cfg leaves you with the reviewed configuration and nothing typed on a
# box. Put the invite in server.cfg instead -- below the `exec "tunables.cfg"`
# line and above `ensure br_lib`, which is where server.cfg.example shows it --
# and it survives every swap between this file and the dev one. Put it here and
# you will lose it the next time somebody makes this box a dev box and back.
#
# Unset is not broken: the player is told why they were removed, and no appeal
# line is printed at all.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
